    "pause_action": "ui.pause",
    "doc": "The native Semu menu the renderer draws over any emulator with a compositor. The supervisor mirrors this list: the same journal drives the drawn selection and the executed action. BEZEL and SHADER step this system's own choice through its variants, then off (confirm or right forward, left back), live and saved as visual.systems.<id>.bezel_variant or shader_variant, never the global switches, which stay the default for systems without their own choice. An action's toast is what the renderer shows for a moment after it runs (SEMU_MENU_TOASTS): {slot} is the slot as the emulator numbers it (SLOT 3), empty with one fixed slot; {label} is the chosen variant's label, OFF for none; any bezel or shader change shows the Next Bezel or Next Shader toast, and a shader that must compile first shows its loading_toast until it is built. pause_action reaches only emulators whose emulator.json menu.pause is emulator (seen to keep presenting while paused); the others keep running under the menu, and an emulator without a compositor gets no menu."
  },
  "gamepad_chords": {
    "modifier": "select",
    "bindings": {
      "north": "ui.menu",
      "east": "ui.screenshot",
      "tr": "state.save",
      "tl": "state.load",
      "dpad_left": "state.prev",
      "dpad_right": "state.next"
    },
    "xpad_layout_ids": [
      "28de:11ff",
      "045e:*"
    ],
    "doc": "The plain-controller paradigm: hold Select and press a button. Start+Select stays the quit chord. Button names are positions (north is the top face button); pads listed in xpad_layout_ids (vendor:product, * for any product) are xpad-ordered and report their top button as BTN_WEST, so the supervisor swaps BTN_NORTH and BTN_WEST for them: Steam's virtual pad (28de:11ff) and Microsoft pads. On the Deck the trackpad radial emits the keyboard chords instead, which reach the supervisor as X raw keys in Game Mode; both paths produce the same actions."
  }
